IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nz-nouns`

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 2, GENERAL DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION PROVISIONS (ss 13 to 23).
-- Every defined term of s 13 has an entry in the glossary module nz-glossary.l4. This module encodes the definitions that
-- decide something from facts, and the rules of reading (ss 14 to 23). s 13's "month" and "working day" are in
-- nz-interpretation-time.l4; s 17 (sending by post) is there too.

§ `Section 13 -- Definitions of terms for all legislation`

DECLARE Territory IS ONE OF
    `the island commonly known as the North Island`
    `an island adjacent to the North Island`
    `the island commonly known as the South Island`
    `an island adjacent to the South Island`
    `another island or territory within the Realm of New Zealand`
    `the self-governing State of the Cook Islands`
    `the self-governing State of Niue`
    `Tokelau`
    `the Ross Dependency`
    `a place outside the Realm of New Zealand`

DECLARE `Which island` IS ONE OF
    `North Island`
    `South Island`
    `Neither island`

-- src:128 | New Zealand or similar words referring to New Zealand, when used as a territorial description,—
-- src:129 | means the islands and territories within the Realm of New Zealand; but
-- src:130 | does not include the self-governing State of the Cook Islands, the self-governing State of Niue, Tokelau, or the Ross Dependency
-- "New Zealand ... when used as a territorial description, means the islands and territories within the Realm of New Zealand; but does
-- not include the self-governing State of the Cook Islands, the self-governing State of Niue, Tokelau, or the Ross Dependency."
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of New Zealand (src:128-130)
GIVEN place IS A Territory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is within New Zealand as a territorial description` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `the island commonly known as the North Island` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an island adjacent to the North Island` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the island commonly known as the South Island` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an island adjacent to the South Island` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another island or territory within the Realm of New Zealand` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the self-governing State of the Cook Islands` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the self-governing State of Niue` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Tokelau` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Ross Dependency` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a place outside the Realm of New Zealand` THEN FALSE

-- "North Island ... means the island commonly known as the North Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it"; likewise the South Island.
-- src:151 | South Island or Te Waipounamu, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the South Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- src:131 | North Island or Te Ika-a-Māui, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the North Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definitions of North Island and South Island (src:131) (src:151)
GIVEN place IS A Territory
GIVETH A `Which island`
`which island the place is, under the Act's definitions` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `the island commonly known as the North Island` THEN `North Island`
    WHEN `an island adjacent to the North Island` THEN `North Island`
    WHEN `the island commonly known as the South Island` THEN `South Island`
    WHEN `an island adjacent to the South Island` THEN `South Island`
    OTHERWISE `Neither island`

-- src:152 | territorial limits of New Zealand, limits of New Zealand, or a similar expression, when used as a territorial description, means the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand
-- "territorial limits of New Zealand ... when used as a territorial description, means the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand".
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of territorial limits of New Zealand (src:152)
GIVETH A STRING
`the territorial limits of New Zealand are` MEANS "the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand"

-- src:134 | person includes a corporation sole, a body corporate, and an unincorporated body
-- "person includes a corporation sole, a body corporate, and an unincorporated body". A natural person is not named: "includes" does
-- not say, so NOTHING (the ordinary meaning is not in the Act).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of person (src:134)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as a person under section 13` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an unincorporated body` THEN JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Kind of ending of legislation` IS ONE OF
    `repeal in the ordinary sense`
    `expiry`
    `another lapsing or ceasing of effect`
    `revocation`
    `replacement`
    `something else`

-- src:145 | repeal, in relation to any legislation, includes—
-- src:146 | expiry (or any other lapsing or ceasing of effect); and
-- src:147 | revocation; and
-- src:148 | replacement
-- "repeal, in relation to any legislation, includes (a) expiry (or any other lapsing or ceasing of effect); and (b) revocation; and (c) replacement".
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of repeal (src:145-148)
GIVEN ending IS A `Kind of ending of legislation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as repeal under section 13` ending MEANS
    CONSIDER ending
    WHEN `repeal in the ordinary sense` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `expiry` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another lapsing or ceasing of effect` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `revocation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `replacement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Publication of a notice` HAS
    `it is published in the Gazette`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is published in one or more newspapers circulating in the area to which the act, matter or thing relates or in which it arises`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is published on an Internet site administered by or on behalf of the person who must or may publish the notice`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Internet site is publicly available as far as practicable`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Internet site is free of charge`                                        IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:141 | public notification, public notice, or a similar expression in relation to an act, a matter, or a thing, means a notice published—
-- src:142 | in the Gazette; or
-- src:143 | in 1 or more newspapers circulating in the area to which the act, matter, or thing relates or in which it arises; or
-- src:144 | on an Internet site that is administered by or on behalf of the person who must or may publish the notice, and that is publicly available as far as practicable and free of charge
-- "public notification, public notice, or a similar expression ... means a notice published (a) in the Gazette; or (b) in 1 or more
-- newspapers circulating in the area ...; or (c) on an Internet site that is administered by or on behalf of the person who must or
-- may publish the notice, and that is publicly available as far as practicable and free of charge".
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of public notification (src:141-144)
GIVEN notice IS A `Publication of a notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is public notification` notice MEANS
        (notice's `it is published in the Gazette`)
     OR (notice's `it is published in one or more newspapers circulating in the area to which the act, matter or thing relates or in which it arises`)
     OR (    (notice's `it is published on an Internet site administered by or on behalf of the person who must or may publish the notice`)
         AND (notice's `the Internet site is publicly available as far as practicable`)
         AND (notice's `the Internet site is free of charge`))

-- src:140 | Proclamation means a Proclamation made and signed by the Governor-General under the Seal of New Zealand and (if it is not legislation) published in the Gazette
-- "Proclamation means a Proclamation made and signed by the Governor-General under the Seal of New Zealand and (if it is not legislation) published in the Gazette".
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of Proclamation (src:140)
GIVEN `it is made and signed by the Governor-General under the Seal of New Zealand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Proclamation` `it is made and signed by the Governor-General under the Seal of New Zealand` `it is legislation` `it is published in the Gazette` MEANS
        `it is made and signed by the Governor-General under the Seal of New Zealand`
    AND (`it is legislation` OR `it is published in the Gazette`)

-- src:137 | proceeding means a proceeding (whether civil, criminal, disciplinary, or other, at any stage, and interlocutory or main)—
-- src:138 | in or before a court or tribunal, or before a person acting judicially; or
-- src:139 | of a person or body performing administrative functions, investigative functions, or both
-- "proceeding means a proceeding (whether civil, criminal, disciplinary, or other, at any stage, and interlocutory or main) (a) in or before a
-- court or tribunal, or before a person acting judicially; or (b) of a person or body performing administrative functions, investigative functions, or both".
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of proceeding (src:137-139)
GIVEN `it is in or before a court or tribunal, or before a person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is of a person or body performing administrative functions, investigative functions, or both` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a proceeding` `it is in or before a court or tribunal, or before a person acting judicially` `it is of a person or body performing administrative functions, investigative functions, or both` MEANS
    `it is in or before a court or tribunal, or before a person acting judicially`
    OR `it is of a person or body performing administrative functions, investigative functions, or both`

DECLARE `Form and medium of words` IS ONE OF
    `in print`
    `written or typed on paper`
    `fixed on a physical object`
    `shown only on a screen`
    `spoken only, or otherwise not visible`

-- src:159 | writing means representing or reproducing words, figures, or symbols in a visible and tangible form and medium (for example, in print) (but see Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017, which provides for meeting written requirements by electronic means).
-- "writing means representing or reproducing words, figures, or symbols in a visible and tangible form and medium (for example, in print) (but see Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017, which provides for meeting written requirements by electronic means)".
-- The form and medium are named by what a person can see: print and other things fixed on paper or an object are visible and tangible; words that are only spoken are not visible; words shown only on a screen are visible, but the Act does not say that a screen
-- is a tangible medium, so the answer for them is NOTHING (not covered), not FALSE.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of writing (src:159)
GIVEN `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `Form and medium of words`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is writing` `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` form MEANS
    IF NOT `it represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER form
         WHEN `in print` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `written or typed on paper` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `fixed on a physical object` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `shown only on a screen` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `spoken only, or otherwise not visible` THEN JUST FALSE

-- "(but see Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 ...)": whether that Part lets a requirement be met electronically is a fact borrowed from that Act and is asked as an input.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of writing (src:159)
GIVEN `it is writing as section 13 defines it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 provides for the requirement to be met by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a requirement to put something in writing is met` `it is writing as section 13 defines it` `Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 provides for the requirement to be met by electronic means` MEANS
    IF `Part 4 of the Contract and Commercial Law Act 2017 provides for the requirement to be met by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `it is writing as section 13 defines it`

§ `Section 13 -- member lookups for the definitions that list things`

-- Section 13 defines many terms by a list. Each lookup below takes one candidate and says whether the definition covers it: the printed phrase is a member, and so is each thing it names (ruling C).
-- A definition that says "means" is CLOSED: a candidate that is off the list is not covered, JUST FALSE. One that says "includes", or "means ... and include", is OPEN: a candidate off the list is neither in nor out, NOTHING.

DECLARE `Candidate for the term Act` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Parliament of New Zealand or of the General Assembly`
    `an Act of the Parliament of New Zealand`
    `an Act of the General Assembly`
    `a regulation`
    `a Bill that has not been enacted`
    `an instrument of another kind`

-- src:111 | Act means an Act—
-- src:112 | of the Parliament of New Zealand; or
-- src:113 | of the General Assembly
-- "Act means an Act of the Parliament of New Zealand; or of the General Assembly". CLOSED ("means").
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of Act (src:111-113)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as an Act under section 13` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an Act of the Parliament of New Zealand or of the General Assembly` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the Parliament of New Zealand` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an Act of the General Assembly` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a regulation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a Bill that has not been enacted` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an instrument of another kind` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for the term enactment` IS ONE OF
    `the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation`
    `the whole of an Act`
    `a part of an Act`
    `any secondary legislation`
    `a Bill before it is enacted`
    `an instrument that is not legislation`

-- src:119 | enactment means the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation
-- "enactment means the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation". CLOSED ("means"): a Bill is not an enactment.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of enactment (src:119)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term enactment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as an enactment under section 13` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `the whole or a part of an Act or any secondary legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the whole of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a part of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any secondary legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Bill before it is enacted` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an instrument that is not legislation` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for the term Gazette` IS ONE OF
    `the New Zealand Gazette (or a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette)`
    `the New Zealand Gazette`
    `a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette`
    `another gazette or journal`

-- src:120 | Gazette means the New Zealand Gazette (or a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette) published or purporting to be published under the authority of the New Zealand Government
-- "Gazette means the New Zealand Gazette (or a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette) published or purporting to be published under the authority of the New Zealand Government". CLOSED ("means"), and the publication condition applies to each.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of Gazette (src:120)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term Gazette`
      `it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as the Gazette under section 13` thing `when it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government:` `it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government` MEANS
    IF `it is published, or purports to be published, under the authority of the New Zealand Government`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
         WHEN `the New Zealand Gazette (or a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `the New Zealand Gazette` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a supplement to the New Zealand Gazette` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `another gazette or journal` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for the term Commonwealth country` IS ONE OF
    `a country that is a member of the Commonwealth`
    `a territory for the international relations of which a member of the Commonwealth is responsible`
    `a place that is neither`

-- src:115 | Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth mean a country that is a member of the Commonwealth; and include a territory for the international relations of which the member is responsible
-- "Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth mean a country that is a member of the Commonwealth; and include a territory for the international relations of which the member is responsible". OPEN ("means ... and include").
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth (src:115)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term Commonwealth country`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as a Commonwealth country or part of the Commonwealth under section 13` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `a country that is a member of the Commonwealth` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a territory for the international relations of which a member of the Commonwealth is responsible` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a place that is neither` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Candidate for the term office` IS ONE OF
    `an office`
    `a position`
    `something else`

-- src:132 | office includes position
-- "office includes position". OPEN ("includes").
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of office (src:132)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as an office under section 13` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an office` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a position` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Candidate for the term Governor-General in Council` IS ONE OF
    `the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council`
    `the Governor-General acting alone`
    `the Executive Council acting alone`
    `anyone else`

-- src:121 | Governor-General in Council or a similar expression means the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council
-- "Governor-General in Council or a similar expression means the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council". CLOSED ("means").
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of Governor-General in Council (src:121)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term Governor-General in Council`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as the Governor-General in Council under section 13` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Governor-General acting alone` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the Executive Council acting alone` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `anyone else` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for the term prescribed` IS ONE OF
    `prescribed by or under legislation`
    `prescribed by legislation`
    `prescribed under legislation`
    `prescribed by regulations`
    `prescribed by a private contract`
    `prescribed by anything else`

-- src:135 | prescribed means prescribed by or under legislation
-- "prescribed means prescribed by or under legislation". CLOSED ("means"): regulations are legislation; a private contract is not.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of prescribed (src:135)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term prescribed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as prescribed under section 13` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `prescribed by or under legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `prescribed by legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `prescribed under legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `prescribed by regulations` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `prescribed by a private contract` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `prescribed by anything else` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for the term department` IS ONE OF
    `the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture named in Part 1, 2 or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020`
    `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020`
    `a departmental agency named in Part 2 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020`
    `an interdepartmental venture named in Part 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020`
    `a body that Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020 does not name`

-- src:118 | department, in relation to any legislation, means the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture (as named in Part 1, 2, or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020) that, with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation
-- src:126 | Ministry, in relation to any legislation, means the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture (as named in Part 1, 2, or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020) that, with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation
-- "department, in relation to any legislation, means the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture (as named in Part 1, 2, or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020) that, with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the
-- administration of the legislation"; "Ministry" has the same words. CLOSED ("means"), and the responsibility condition applies to each. Whether Schedule 2 names the body is a borrowed fact: the candidate is the input.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definitions of department and Ministry (src:118) (src:126)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term department`
      `it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as the department or Ministry under section 13` thing `when it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation:` `it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation` MEANS
    IF `it is responsible, with the authority of the Prime Minister, for the administration of the legislation`
    THEN CONSIDER thing
         WHEN `the department, departmental agency, or interdepartmental venture named in Part 1, 2 or 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a departmental agency named in Part 2 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an interdepartmental venture named in Part 4 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a body that Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020 does not name` THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Candidate for the term Minister` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister of the Crown who, under the authority of a warrant or with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation`
    `a Minister of the Crown who is responsible for the administration of the legislation under the authority of a warrant`
    `a Minister of the Crown who is responsible for the administration of the legislation with the authority of the Prime Minister`
    `a Minister of the Crown who is not responsible for the administration of the legislation`
    `a person who is not a Minister of the Crown`

-- src:125 | Minister, in relation to any legislation, means the Minister of the Crown who, under the authority of a warrant or with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation
-- "Minister, in relation to any legislation, means the Minister of the Crown who, under the authority of a warrant or with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation".
-- CLOSED ("means"): the two ways of being authorised are each a member, and so is the printed phrase; a Minister who is not responsible, and anyone who is not a Minister of the Crown, are off the list.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of Minister (src:125)
GIVEN thing IS A `Candidate for the term Minister`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`counts as the Minister under section 13` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `the Minister of the Crown who, under the authority of a warrant or with the authority of the Prime Minister, is responsible for the administration of the legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Minister of the Crown who is responsible for the administration of the legislation under the authority of a warrant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Minister of the Crown who is responsible for the administration of the legislation with the authority of the Prime Minister` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Minister of the Crown who is not responsible for the administration of the legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a person who is not a Minister of the Crown` THEN JUST FALSE

-- The names a definition of section 13 is given under. A definition that says "or a similar expression" (or "or similar words") reaches expressions like the ones it names, so it is OPEN to them; the answer is the
-- headword of the definition that covers the expression, or NOTHING when no definition in section 13 names it. The alternative names of the two islands are official (Te Ika-a-Māui and Te Waipounamu).
DECLARE `Expression used in legislation` IS ONE OF
    `public notification`
    `public notice`
    `an expression similar to public notification`
    `Governor-General in Council`
    `an expression similar to Governor-General in Council`
    `New Zealand`
    `words similar to New Zealand`
    `territorial limits of New Zealand`
    `limits of New Zealand`
    `an expression similar to territorial limits of New Zealand`
    `North Island`
    `Te Ika-a-Māui`
    `South Island`
    `Te Waipounamu`
    `Commonwealth country`
    `part of the Commonwealth`
    `an expression that no definition in section 13 names`

-- src:115 | Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth mean a country that is a member of the Commonwealth; and include a territory for the international relations of which the member is responsible
-- src:121 | Governor-General in Council or a similar expression means the Governor-General acting on the advice and with the consent of the Executive Council
-- src:128 | New Zealand or similar words referring to New Zealand, when used as a territorial description,—
-- src:131 | North Island or Te Ika-a-Māui, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the North Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- src:141 | public notification, public notice, or a similar expression in relation to an act, a matter, or a thing, means a notice published—
-- src:151 | South Island or Te Waipounamu, both official alternative names, means the island commonly known as the South Island, and includes the islands adjacent to it
-- src:152 | territorial limits of New Zealand, limits of New Zealand, or a similar expression, when used as a territorial description, means the outer limits of the territorial sea of New Zealand
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definitions of public notification, Governor-General in Council, New Zealand, North Island, South Island, territorial limits of New Zealand, Commonwealth country (src:115) (src:121) (src:128) (src:131) (src:141) (src:151) (src:152)
GIVEN expression IS AN `Expression used in legislation`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the headword of the section 13 definition that covers` expression MEANS
    CONSIDER expression
    WHEN `public notification` THEN JUST "public notification"
    WHEN `public notice` THEN JUST "public notification"
    WHEN `an expression similar to public notification` THEN JUST "public notification"
    WHEN `Governor-General in Council` THEN JUST "Governor-General in Council"
    WHEN `an expression similar to Governor-General in Council` THEN JUST "Governor-General in Council"
    WHEN `New Zealand` THEN JUST "New Zealand"
    WHEN `words similar to New Zealand` THEN JUST "New Zealand"
    WHEN `territorial limits of New Zealand` THEN JUST "territorial limits of New Zealand"
    WHEN `limits of New Zealand` THEN JUST "territorial limits of New Zealand"
    WHEN `an expression similar to territorial limits of New Zealand` THEN JUST "territorial limits of New Zealand"
    WHEN `North Island` THEN JUST "North Island"
    WHEN `Te Ika-a-Māui` THEN JUST "North Island"
    WHEN `South Island` THEN JUST "South Island"
    WHEN `Te Waipounamu` THEN JUST "South Island"
    WHEN `Commonwealth country` THEN JUST "Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth"
    WHEN `part of the Commonwealth` THEN JUST "Commonwealth country and part of the Commonwealth"
    WHEN `an expression that no definition in section 13 names` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 14 -- Meaning of de facto relationship`

DECLARE `Relationship between two people` HAS
    `the age of the first person in years`   IS A NUMBER
    `the age of the second person in years`  IS A NUMBER
    `they live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `they are married to, or in a civil union with, each other`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `each person aged 16 or 17 has obtained consent under section 46A of the Care of Children Act 2004`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:160 | 14 Meaning of de facto relationship
-- src:161 | In any legislation, de facto relationship means a relationship between 2 people (regardless of their sex, sexual orientation, or gender identity) who—
-- src:162 | live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union; and
-- src:163 | are not married to, or in a civil union with, each other; and
-- src:164 | are both aged 16 years or older.
-- src:165 | However, a relationship involving a person aged 16 or 17 years is not a de facto relationship unless that person has obtained consent for the relationship in accordance with section 46A of the Care of Children Act 2004.
-- (1) a relationship between 2 people (regardless of their sex, sexual orientation, or gender identity) who live together as a couple in a
-- relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union; are not married to, or in a civil union with, each other; and are both aged 16 or older.
-- (2) a relationship involving a person aged 16 or 17 is not a de facto relationship unless that person has obtained consent under s 46A
-- of the Care of Children Act 2004 (a borrowed rule: the consent is an input). "Live together as a couple" is a judgment (see (3)): an input.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 14(1) and (2) (src:160-165)
GIVEN relationship IS A `Relationship between two people`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a de facto relationship` relationship MEANS
        (relationship's `they live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union`)
    AND (NOT (relationship's `they are married to, or in a civil union with, each other`))
    AND (relationship's `the age of the first person in years` AT LEAST 16)
    AND (relationship's `the age of the second person in years` AT LEAST 16)
    AND (    (    (relationship's `the age of the first person in years` AT LEAST 18)
              AND (relationship's `the age of the second person in years` AT LEAST 18))
          OR (relationship's `each person aged 16 or 17 has obtained consent under section 46A of the Care of Children Act 2004`))

-- (3) in deciding whether 2 people live together as a couple, the court or person must have regard to the context and purpose of the law
-- in or for which the question is to be determined, and all the circumstances of the relationship.
-- src:166 | In determining whether 2 people live together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union, the court or person required to determine the question must have regard to—
-- src:168 | all the circumstances of the relationship.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 14(3) (src:166-168)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`what must be had regard to in deciding whether 2 people live together as a couple` MEANS
    LIST "the context, and the purpose of the law, in or for which the question is to be determined", "all the circumstances of the relationship"

-- (4) A de facto relationship ends if the partners cease living together as a couple, or one of them dies.
-- src:169 | A de facto relationship ends if—
-- src:171 | one of the de facto partners dies.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 14(4) (src:169-171)
GIVEN `the partners cease living together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the de facto partners dies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a de facto relationship ends` `the partners cease living together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union` `one of the de facto partners dies` MEANS
    `the partners cease living together as a couple in a relationship in the nature of marriage or civil union` OR `one of the de facto partners dies`

-- s 13: "de facto partner means a person who is a party to a de facto relationship (as defined in section 14)".
-- src:117 | de facto partner means a person who is a party to a de facto relationship (as defined in section 14)
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 13, definition of de facto partner (src:117)
GIVEN relationship IS A `Relationship between two people`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both people are de facto partners` relationship MEANS `is a de facto relationship` relationship

§ `Section 15 -- Meaning of step-parent, etc`

DECLARE `How a relationship arose` IS ONE OF
    `marriage`
    `civil union`
    `de facto relationship`
    `none of these`

-- src:172 | 15 Meaning of step-parent, etc
-- src:173 | The relationship of step-parent, stepson, stepdaughter, or any other relationship described by a word containing the prefix step, may be established by civil union or by de facto relationship as well as by marriage.
-- A step relationship "may be established by civil union or by de facto relationship as well as by marriage". Nothing else is named: NOTHING.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 15 (src:172-173)
GIVEN basis IS A `How a relationship arose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a step relationship may be established by` basis MEANS
    CONSIDER basis
    WHEN `marriage` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `civil union` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `de facto relationship` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 16 -- References to specific gender or kind of person include others`

DECLARE `Words denoting` IS ONE OF
    `a gender`
    `a natural person by referring to a gender or to persons generally`
    `a corporation sole, a body corporate or an unincorporated body`
    `a corporation sole`
    `a body corporate`
    `an unincorporated body`

DECLARE Gender IS ONE OF
    `the male gender`
    `the female gender`
    `any other gender`

-- src:174 | 16 References to specific gender or kind of person include others
-- src:175 | Words denoting a gender include every other gender.
-- (1) Words denoting a gender include every other gender: whatever the gender a word denotes, it includes each of the others.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 16(1) (src:174-175)
GIVEN denoted IS A Gender
      other IS A Gender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words denoting the gender` denoted `include the gender` other MEANS TRUE

-- (2) Words denoting a natural person (he or she, someone, people) include a corporation sole, a body corporate and an unincorporated body
-- if capable of referring to one. (3) Words denoting one of those include a natural person if capable of referring to one.
-- src:176 | Words denoting a natural person by referring to a gender (for example, he or she) or words referring to persons generally (for example, someone or people) include a corporation sole, a body corporate, and an unincorporated body if capable of referring to a corporation sole, a body corporate, or an unincorporated body.
-- src:177 | Words denoting a corporation sole, a body corporate, or an unincorporated body include a natural person if capable of referring to a natural person.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 16(2) and (3) (src:176-177)
GIVEN denoting IS A `Words denoting`
      included IS A `Kind of person`
      `the words are capable of referring to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`words denoting` denoting `include` included `if capable of referring to it` `the words are capable of referring to it` MEANS
    CONSIDER denoting
    WHEN `a gender` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a natural person by referring to a gender or to persons generally` THEN
        CONSIDER included
        WHEN `a natural person` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST `the words are capable of referring to it`
    WHEN `a corporation sole, a body corporate or an unincorporated body` THEN
        CONSIDER included
        WHEN `a natural person` THEN JUST `the words are capable of referring to it`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN
        CONSIDER included
        WHEN `a natural person` THEN JUST `the words are capable of referring to it`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN
        CONSIDER included
        WHEN `a natural person` THEN JUST `the words are capable of referring to it`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `an unincorporated body` THEN
        CONSIDER included
        WHEN `a natural person` THEN JUST `the words are capable of referring to it`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 18 -- Parts of speech have corresponding meaning`

-- src:184 | 18 Parts of speech have corresponding meaning
-- src:185 | Parts of speech and grammatical forms of a word that is defined in any legislation have corresponding meanings in the same legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 18 (src:184-185)
GIVEN `the form is of a word defined in the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is used in the same legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a part of speech or grammatical form has a corresponding meaning` `the form is of a word defined in the legislation` `the form is used in the same legislation` MEANS
    `the form is of a word defined in the legislation` AND `the form is used in the same legislation`

§ `Section 19 -- Words in singular include plural and vice versa`

-- src:186 | 19 Words in singular include plural and vice versa
-- src:187 | Words in the singular include the plural, and words in the plural include the singular.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 19 (src:186-187)
GIVEN written IS A `Number of a word`
      included IS A `Number of a word`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words in the` written `number include the` included `number` MEANS TRUE

§ `Section 20 -- Words used in secondary legislation or other instruments have the same meaning as in the empowering legislation`

-- src:188 | 20 Words used in secondary legislation or other instruments have same meaning as in empowering legislation
-- src:189 | A word or an expression used in secondary legislation, or in any instrument, has the same meaning as it has, from time to time, in the legislation under which the secondary legislation or instrument is made.
-- The word has the same meaning as it has "from time to time" in the legislation under which the instrument is made: the meaning
-- in the empowering legislation at the time asked about, not the meaning when the instrument was made.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 20 (src:188-189)
GIVEN `the meaning in the empowering legislation when the instrument was made` IS A STRING
      `the meaning in the empowering legislation at the time asked about` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the meaning of a word used in secondary legislation or an instrument` `the meaning in the empowering legislation when the instrument was made` `the meaning in the empowering legislation at the time asked about` MEANS
    `the meaning in the empowering legislation at the time asked about`

§ `Section 21 -- Anything done under secondary legislation or other instrument is also done under the Act`

-- src:190 | 21 Anything done under secondary legislation or other instrument is also done under Act
-- src:191 | A reference to anything being done under an Act includes anything done under secondary legislation, or another instrument, that is made under that Act.
-- src:192 | Example
-- src:193 | An Act empowers regulations to authorise a regulator to set fees. The Act requires all fees paid under the Act to be paid to the Crown. The regulations require the regulator to set fees by issuing a notice. The fees set in the regulator’s notice are paid under the Act and so must be paid to the Crown.
-- "A reference to anything being done under an Act includes anything done under secondary legislation, or another instrument, that is made under that Act."
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 21 (src:190-191) (src:193)
GIVEN `it is done under secondary legislation or another instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is done under the Act` `it is done under secondary legislation or another instrument` `the instrument is made under the Act` MEANS
    `it is done under secondary legislation or another instrument` AND `the instrument is made under the Act`

§ `Section 22 -- Legislation not binding on the Crown`

-- src:194 | 22 Legislation not binding on the Crown
-- src:195 | No Act or part of an Act binds the Crown unless the Act (or other legislation) expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or part.
-- (1) No Act or part of an Act binds the Crown unless the Act (or other legislation) expressly provides that the Crown is bound.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 22(1) (src:194-195)
GIVEN `legislation expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or the part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act or part of an Act binds the Crown` `legislation expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or the part` MEANS
    `legislation expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or the part`

-- (2) No secondary legislation, or part of it, binds the Crown unless (a) the Act (or another Act) expressly provides that the Crown is bound
-- by the Act or part under which it is made; or (b) the Act or the secondary legislation (or any other legislation) expressly provides that
-- the Crown is bound by the secondary legislation or part.
-- src:196 | No secondary legislation, or part of secondary legislation, made under an Act or part of an Act binds the Crown unless—
-- src:198 | the Act or the secondary legislation (or any other legislation) expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the secondary legislation or part of the secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 22(2) (src:196-198)
GIVEN `an Act expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or part under which it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `legislation expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the secondary legislation or part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`secondary legislation or a part of it binds the Crown` `an Act expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or part under which it is made` `legislation expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the secondary legislation or part` MEANS
    `an Act expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the Act or part under which it is made`
    OR `legislation expressly provides that the Crown is bound by the secondary legislation or part`

§ `Section 23 -- Examples do not limit provision`

-- src:199 | 23 Examples do not limit provision
-- src:200 | An example provided in legislation of the operation of a provision of the legislation does not limit the provision.
-- src:201 | See section 10, which includes examples as part of the text of legislation from which its meaning must be ascertained.
-- "An example provided in legislation of the operation of a provision of the legislation does not limit the provision." Section 10 makes
-- the example part of the text from which meaning is ascertained; section 23 says it does not narrow the provision. (Schedule 1 clause 4
-- takes pre-commencement examples out of this section: see nz-schedules.l4.)
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 23 (src:199-201)
GIVEN `the example is provided in legislation of the operation of a provision of that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an example limits the provision` `the example is provided in legislation of the operation of a provision of that legislation` MEANS
    IF `the example is provided in legislation of the operation of a provision of that legislation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING
